	// #100: THE MANIFEST IS THE PAYLOAD. It names the tagged release's
	// toplevel store path; `nanokvm-update` substitutes that closure from our
	// signed binary cache, fetching only what this device does not already
	// have. So nothing is downloaded, hashed or untarred here -- the three
	// steps that used to stand between the version check and install() are
	// gone, and with them the 460 MB tarball they moved
	// (pkgs/nanokvm-server.nix step 3b).
	//
	// #101: AND NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE EITHER. update() used to ask upstream's
	// version check first, from a URL compiled into this binary, while install()
	// hands off to `nanokvm-update`, which reads the channel the DEVICE is
	// configured with -- two sources of truth for one press of the button, and
	// the compiled one 404ed. `install-now` fetches the manifest for the
	// device's channel itself and refuses if there is nothing to install, so
	// the pre-check bought nothing but a second way to fail.
	_ = sendMessage("install", 0)
	err := install("", "")
